<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yakubu of Bauchi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1845">1845</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Yaqub of Bauchi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yakubu was the founder and first emir of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bauchi">Bauchi</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>. A Gerawa scholar and student of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/usman-dan-fodio">Usman dan Fodio</a>, he was the only one of the original flag-bearers of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jihad">jihad</a> who was not a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fula">Fulani</a>. He founded the town of Bauchi around 1809 and ruled for about forty years, expanding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> by conquest.</p></div>
